Fig. 85.10 Illustration of a “distal perfusion cannula” in the femoral artery. The extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (ECMO) arterial 
cannula is placed in the artery and advanced to the internal iliac artery; 
the distal perfusion cannula is placed distal to the arterial ECMO cannula, aiming down the leg to provide additional perfusion.
